# pinch (M9): a trackpad's pinch over the plane. A browser hands it to the page as wheel events with
# Ctrl held, −100 ln(scale) px each (Chromium's convention), and the plane zooms on them as on any
# wheel, about the pointer, by exp(−deltaY · 0.0015): `pinch 1.2840254166877416` is −25 px (whole,
# as WebKit delivers a wheel), so 50 · exp(0.0375) = 51.91 px a unit; natively it is SDL's own pinch
# event of that scale, read the same way. Then a Ctrl + wheel of −50 px (natively a wheel with Ctrl
# held, in a browser a pinch that web/library.js reads back as a scale): 50 · exp(0.1125) = 55.95.
# The pointer at (1106, 338) at 1440 x 900, 150 px right of the plane's centre and 150 above, keeps
# its maths under it. Chromium hands the wheel over at half its delta, on the reference too.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
move 1106 338
wait 500
pinch 1.2840254166877416
wait 16
shot pinch
wheel 0 -50 ctrl
wait 16
shot ctrl-wheel
